							<Item class="Script" referent="RBX5400">
								<Properties>
									<bool name="Disabled">false</bool>
									<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
									<string name="Name">HF Guide (DOUBLE CLICK THIS)</string>
									<ProtectedString name="Source">HF Organization Member's manual

This is not a Script.

If At a base like Fort Miranda, In case of an enemy attack, head to the nearest battlestation, or the nearest aircraft. Close the gates and
DO NOT LET ANYONE IN

If evacuating, evacuate the most people your evac craft can carry.

At a HF Organization base, DO NOT let a Non HF member into the armory areas, unless instructed
by a Union Officer.

Always respect your officers.
TEAMKILLING WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED.

Don't kill anyone trying to enter the base, unless it's a hostile. 

Always have a small arms weapon in case of an enemy attack.

In this organization, The Air Force was merged into the Space Force. 

-------------------------------------------------------------

Refer to these codes at all times at an HF Base:

Condition Green: No enemy attack
Condition Yellow: On alert, No enemy attack
Condition Amber:  Expecting Enemy attack, High alert
Condition Orange- Invasion confirmed, Light enemy attack
Condition Red: Heavy Enemy Attack, Full defense effort
--------------------------------------------------------------
Ranks of the HF Organization

Grand Chancellor- Leader of the Organization. Has control over the Organization.
Vice Chancellor- Leader of the Organization at Grand Chancellor's absence
Grand Admiral- Leader of the Air and Space Force
Master General- Leader of the Army
Clan Relations officer- Leader position held by one person. Responsible for clan peace relations.

Armed Ground Forces Ranks

The armed Ground Forces balances battles by establishing ground dominance. without them, the Air and space forces will have to face 
Surface to air attacks. 

5- Star General- Lead Officer that is usually assigned espionage missions.
4- Star General- Lead Officer that is one below the bigtime.
3-Star General- Lead Officer that handles Peace treaties aboard the Ariadne-Class.
2-Star General- Lead Officer over a Battalion (HF Battalion-40 troops)
1-Star General- Lead officer over a Company (HF Company- 20 Troops)
Brigadier General- Leader of a Major Platoon (HF Major platoon- 15 troops)
Liutenant-Colonel- Lead officer of a Platoon (HF Platoon- (10 troops)
Colonel- Lead officer of a support Platoon (8 troops)
Liutenant- Lead Officer of a 4th Class Squadron (6 troops)
2nd Liutenant- Second in command of a 3rd class squadron
1st Liutenant- Commander of a 2nd Class squadron (4 troops)
Captain- Commander of a 1st class squadron (2 troops)
Command Warrant officer- capable
Warrant Officer- capable of approving defenses and light to medium attacks.
Corporal- Follows that Captain or other commanding officers
Sgt. Major- Follows the Corporal or other commanding officers
Sgt. Second Class- Follows the Corporal or other commanding officers
Sgt. First Class- Follows the Corporal or other commanding officers
Staff Sergeant- Follows corporal or other commanding officers
Sergeant- Follows the Corporal or other commanding officers
Brigadier Private- Follows the Corporal or other commanding officers
Private- Follows the Corporal or other commanding officers

Air and Space Force Ranks

The Air and Space Force is the main force that balances battles by dominating air, sea, or space dominance.
Without them, the ground forces are vulnerable from air attacks.

Union Command Officer- Hand picked by the Grand Chancellor from the finest admirals. Leads an Armada.
Admiral- Leader of a fleet. Assigned to the Flagship.
Rear admiral- Vice to the Admiral. Assigned to the Flagship.
Major Commodore- Commands a large vessel (i.e, Cruiser, Battlecruiser, or even a battleship.)
Commodore- Commands a medium vessel(i.e, Destroyer , Missile Destroyer, or an AEGIS Frigate.)
Minor Commodore- Commands a small vessel (i.e, Frigate, Missile frigate, Tender ship, or Medical ship)
Captain- Leader of an air squadron.
Liutenant- Rank required to fly bombers.
2nd Liutenant- Rank required to fly advanced fighters.
1st liutenant- Minimum rank required to fly an aircraft. Usually the trainee.
Airman 1st Class- Trainee almost ready to fly a small fighter.
Airman 2nd Class- Trainee that should learn the basics of fighter training
Ensign- Minor officer.
Crewman- Lowest rank in the Air and Space Force. Should know the basic repair for aircraft.

Civil Protection Forces

Union Protection Officer- Hand Picked by the Grand Chancellor.
Captain- Leader of the security force in the base, or city.
Patrol Ranger-  Ranger in charge of a small outpost.
Command Enforcer- Commander of a security squad (3 troopers)
Major Enforcer- Tactical Assault (TA) trooper.
Enforcer- Basic armoured police officer
Minor Enforcer- Basic rank for a security trooper.
---------------------------------------------------------------
Format:

Code- Explanation

ComOf? - is there a Commanding Officer?
ComofN- No commanding officer
ComofY -Yes, there is a commanding officer
Ensur- Enemy has surrendered
RetFull- Full Retreat
MF-Mission Failed
MA-Mission Accomplished
Corpsman up!- I'm Hit! Medic!
ForAtt- Forward attack Charge
FlaMnR/L- Flanking Maneuver Right / Left
IDSpe- HF Spy
ID01- Grand Chancellor
ID02- Vice Chancellor
ID03- Grand Admiral
ID04- Union Officer
SAF- Small Arms Fire
ComWarn- Combat Warning


------------------------------------------------------------------

List of retired HF Air/Spacecraft
AHP-21A "Spear"- Multirole HF Attack weapons platform.
HP-21B "Sword"- Multirole HF Gunship
ACP-20 "Scimitar" - Gunner platform
HP-170 "Atlas" - Heavy duty transport
